1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,945
Business Case 02 begins when talent marketing defines an audience or
recruiting event.

2
00:00:05,945 --> 00:00:10,518
A consented application retains its campaign, event and source-touch
lineage.

3
00:00:10,518 --> 00:00:12,804
The governed record is CAM-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:17,834
The accountable actors are Talent Marketer, Campus Recruiter, Candidate,
Recruiting Coordinator.

5
00:00:17,834 --> 00:00:24,693
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:24,693 --> 00:00:29,077
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:29,077 --> 00:00:36,968
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:36,968 --> 00:00:41,352
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:41,352 --> 00:00:44,422
Process 1, Talent Marketer: Build eligible audience.

10
00:00:44,422 --> 00:00:50,999
The action apply segment rules produces eligible and suppressed
population snapshot in the Recruiting CRM.

11
00:00:50,999 --> 00:00:54,507
Process 2, Campus Recruiter: Configure event and campaign.

12
00:00:54,507 --> 00:01:00,646
The action bind event to campaign produces versioned event invitation in
the Campaign ledger.

13
00:01:00,646 --> 00:01:03,277
Process 3, Candidate: Register with consent.

14
00:01:03,277 --> 00:01:09,855
The action register or join waitlist produces registration or waitlist
position in the Relationship ledger.

15
00:01:09,855 --> 00:01:12,486
Process 4, Candidate: Start attributed application.

16
00:01:12,486 --> 00:01:19,940
The action follow source-bound job link produces draft application with
immutable source touch in the Application ledger.

17
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,787
The actual product route is /hr/talent/campaigns.

18
00:01:22,787 --> 00:01:29,428
It presents audience, consent and source-attribution builder in the
surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:29,428 --> 00:01:41,289
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:41,289 --> 00:01:44,595
The seeded workbench follows record AUD-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:44,595 --> 00:01:57,820
Its governed fields are Community, Design leaders — Bay Area;
Population, 215 prospects; Eligible, 184; Suppressed, 27 ,
consent/retention; Event, EVT-DEMO-001; Source token,
SRC-CAM-2026-08-PD.

22
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:08,290
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

23
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:11,729
With Recruiter selected, we perform activate eligible audience snapshot.

24
00:02:11,729 --> 00:02:16,313
The guard requires purpose, consent, suppression and effective-date
rules pass per row.

25
00:02:16,313 --> 00:02:26,628
The state changes from Draft population to Activated · 184 eligible,
records AudienceActivated, writes to the Recruiting CRM, and creates the
handoff: Event team receives consented audience.

26
00:02:26,628 --> 00:02:31,530
We now exercise the controlled exception: Expire consent for selected
rows.

27
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:36,433
The prepared failure is 27 records suppressed; 4 have expired authority.

28
00:02:36,433 --> 00:02:45,793
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

29
00:02:45,793 --> 00:02:48,390
The owned recovery is Re-evaluate suppression.

30
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:52,718
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

31
00:02:52,718 --> 00:02:58,345
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

32
00:02:58,345 --> 00:03:07,867
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through eligible, suppressed and attributed conversion rates and
minimum-context next-actor work.

33
00:03:07,867 --> 00:03:10,071
Business Case 02 is complete.

34
00:03:10,071 --> 00:03:22,855
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

35
00:03:22,855 --> 00:03:27,263
A consented application retains its campaign, event and source-touch
lineage.

36
00:03:27,263 --> 00:03:32,112
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
